  "review": [
    "Previous goal turn restored eleven native calls and verified their compiled operands; it was progress. This turn refreshes the full report and validates all 160 explicit source-address bindings before further edits.",
    "The fresh report has 18,828 ranges: 12,466 exact, 270 effective, 6,092 different. Thirteen of the preceding seventeen source owners now compare exactly; the tiny-diff discovery queue has 395 entries. These scores precede the two changes in this record.",
    "The repeated-caller scan examines all 6,078 eligible nonexact ranges. It stops at incoming branch targets as well as outgoing branches/calls. A linear predecessor can prepare values for a different path into a shared call; complete per-call-site counts do not prove path equivalence.",
    "Goblin Tutor, damage_effects and Timecrafting were false positives from shared call blocks. Their allegedly absent 0x38, 0x76 and 0x85 operands already occur in the native code. The block-aware scan retains only Cruel Revival, which also has the native prompt and one unambiguous call.",
    "The readonly-string scan ignores 75 diagnostic line-number changes and finds the formatter selector absent from both current literals and current function immediates. The captured typed decompilation is a reading aid; the native call and selector bytes are checked before editing.",
    "Every formatter token starts with +, -, |, / or backslash. Native strchr excludes only ordinary-copy characters; all signed-zero and single-number formatting paths are retained. This restores a source-level fast path rather than introducing stack/register matching tricks.",
    "The branch survey leaves byte-derived nonnegative loops and paired predicate inversions unchanged. resolve_gfp_ability explicitly returns either zero or a positive pending value, so Midnight Entourage's unsigned/nonzero spelling is not treated as a new bug.",
    "One combined build and focused checks follow. The fresh full comparison becomes a historical snapshot after that build; no post-edit full-match score is claimed."
  ],
